WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.040 --> 00:00:06.640
[Music] Human beings flourish
when they have power to direct the&nbsp;

00:00:06.640 --> 00:00:11.360
course of their own life.
The best way to have access to that&nbsp;

00:00:11.360 --> 00:00:16.320
power is through participation in a
constitutional democracy.&nbsp;

00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:20.000
But democracy survives only if its
citizens

00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:21.840
know how to participate,

00:00:23.760 --> 00:00:26.639
want to participate, 

00:00:26.639 --> 00:00:27.680
have the skills to participate.

00:00:29.520 --> 00:00:31.440
Constitutional democracy is a living

00:00:31.440 --> 00:00:33.760
activity, not something simply to learn

00:00:33.760 --> 00:00:34.560
about on paper.

00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:37.200
This isn't an old-fashioned civics class

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:39.040
where you learn a bunch of information

00:00:39.040 --> 00:00:41.760
about things that are distant from your life.

00:00:41.760 --> 00:00:43.680
This is about putting yourself, as a

00:00:43.680 --> 00:00:45.520
learner, in the position of an

00:00:45.520 --> 00:00:47.680
active civic participant who needs to

00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:49.520
know what you care about and how things work

00:00:50.080 --> 00:00:52.080
in order to shape your own civic journey.

00:00:53.120 --> 00:00:54.480
We'll still cover the traditional

00:00:54.480 --> 00:00:56.960
disciplinary content: think separation of

00:00:56.960 --> 00:00:59.040
powers and checks and balances.

00:00:59.040 --> 00:01:00.400
You'll need to learn about rights and

00:01:00.400 --> 00:01:02.880
responsibilities, constitutionalism,

00:01:02.880 --> 00:01:04.638
the philosophical foundations of democracy,

00:01:04.638 --> 00:01:06.320
and the levers of change.

00:01:06.960 --> 00:01:09.280
But, we will also ask you to put your

00:01:09.280 --> 00:01:10.944
learning into action.

00:01:10.944 --> 00:01:12.080
You'll work from your

00:01:12.080 --> 00:01:13.680
understanding of yourself,

00:01:13.680 --> 00:01:15.280
and your understanding of constitutional

00:01:15.280 --> 00:01:18.042
democracy and the American political community,

00:01:18.080 --> 00:01:20.240
to develop your own theory of change and

00:01:20.240 --> 00:01:21.600
civic action project.

00:01:23.120 --> 00:01:26.640
Healthy democracies depend on citizens

00:01:27.280 --> 00:01:29.040
loving democracy and having the

00:01:29.040 --> 00:01:30.800
knowledge and skills they need

00:01:30.800 --> 00:01:33.200
to play their role as civic participants.

00:01:34.400 --> 00:01:37.947
You can't sit back in a constitutional democracy.

00:01:38.480 --> 00:01:43.019
Your civic actions are just beginning.

